WEBVTT

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/11-0
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.046
<v Jordan Lee>Okay, recording's on. Tom, thanks. This is Quarry Lane Foods.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/12-0
00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:08.823
<v Tom Brennan>Yep. This one's a loss to Spendgrid, unfortunately.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/13-0
00:00:09.523 --> 00:00:14.908
<v Jordan Lee>Okay. Let's walk through it. What happened at Quarry Lane that started this evaluation?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/14-0
00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:33.300
<v Tom Brennan>They bought a smaller company, a bakery brand called Hollow Oak, about a year ago. So now they've got two entities, and the CFO, Linda Moreau, was doing the consolidation by hand. And on top of that their AP was a mess. Lots of paper invoices.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/15-0
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.462
<v Jordan Lee>How do you know the acquisition was the trigger?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/16-0
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:51.238
<v Tom Brennan>Linda said it on the discovery call. She said, "I'm running two companies' books in one spreadsheet." And she said it got really bad after the acquisition closed. So I'd say that's the trigger.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/17-0
00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:56.169
<v Jordan Lee>Great. Who made the final call, and how do you know?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/18-0
00:00:56.869 --> 00:01:11.869
<v Tom Brennan>Linda was the decision maker for the evaluation. She ran it. But the final, final call... so, Linda told me on our last call that anything new had to go to the CEO, Paul Strand, because of the restructuring.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/19-0
00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:14.069
<v Jordan Lee>What restructuring?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/20-0
00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:26.308
<v Tom Brennan>They did layoffs in October. About ten percent. Linda mentioned it like it was no big deal, but after that the CEO had to sign off on all new software.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/21-0
00:01:27.008 --> 00:01:30.854
<v Jordan Lee>Okay. What did the customer bring up about the competitor?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/22-0
00:01:31.554 --> 00:01:42.323
<v Tom Brennan>Spendgrid was in. Linda told me in week two, "We're also looking at Spendgrid, our AP lead likes their invoice module." The AP lead is Carla, Carla Mendes.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/23-0
00:01:43.023 --> 00:01:46.485
<v Jordan Lee>What changed in their questions after they'd met Spendgrid?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/24-0
00:01:47.185 --> 00:01:57.185
<v Tom Brennan>A lot more about AP. Invoice capture, OCR, how do we handle invoices that come in on paper. Before that it was mostly consolidation and close.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/25-0
00:01:57.885 --> 00:02:01.346
<v Jordan Lee>And how do you know they went with Spendgrid?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/26-0
00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:04.738
<v Tom Brennan>Well, they went dark. Linda stopped answering.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/27-0
00:02:05.438 --> 00:02:09.285
<v Jordan Lee>Did anyone at Quarry Lane tell you they picked Spendgrid?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/28-0
00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:38.446
<v Tom Brennan>...No. No one actually said that. I assumed. Actually, now that you ask... Linda's last email said, let me pull it up... "We're pushing this to next fiscal year. Budget is frozen after the restructuring. I'll reach back out in the spring." And I saw on LinkedIn a couple of weeks ago that Carla posted a job for an AP specialist, and the posting said "advanced Excel required." So... maybe they didn't buy anything.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/29-0
00:02:39.146 --> 00:02:47.223
<v Jordan Lee>That's a big difference. Let's keep that in mind. Which part of our pitch got a reaction, and which got silence?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/30-0
00:02:47.923 --> 00:02:58.308
<v Tom Brennan>The thirty-day implementation. Linda's eyebrows went up. She said, "Thirty days, really?" and asked me to send the implementation plan. That was the strongest reaction I got.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/31-0
00:02:59.008 --> 00:03:00.508
<v Jordan Lee>What else?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/32-0
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:13.131
<v Tom Brennan>Carla liked the spend view by vendor, she asked a few questions. The controls and audit stuff got nothing. Total silence. They're private, no audit pressure, I don't think they care.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/33-0
00:03:13.831 --> 00:03:18.446
<v Jordan Lee>When did you first feel this was lost? What happened right before?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/34-0
00:03:19.146 --> 00:03:31.838
<v Tom Brennan>When the restructuring got announced. Mid-October. Before that Linda was responsive, we had a pricing call scheduled. After that she went quiet. She cancelled the pricing call and I couldn't get her back.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/35-0
00:03:32.538 --> 00:03:35.615
<v Jordan Lee>So what's the real reason this didn't close?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/36-0
00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:50.931
<v Tom Brennan>Hmm. I mean, I came in here saying Spendgrid. But honestly, it sounds like the budget got frozen and the deal just stalled. Spendgrid might have been ahead on AP, but I don't actually know that they won.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/37-0
00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:55.092
<v Jordan Lee>What did they ask for that we couldn't show?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/38-0
00:03:55.792 --> 00:04:16.946
<v Tom Brennan>Invoice capture on their actual invoices. Carla wanted to send us a stack of their supplier invoices and see how we read them. A lot of them come from farms, some are handwritten. Our invoice capture is pretty new, and the SE said handwritten wasn't something we could demo confidently. So we didn't do it.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/39-0
00:04:17.646 --> 00:04:22.262
<v Jordan Lee>Okay. Last one. What exact words did they use for their problem?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/40-0
00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:36.808
<v Tom Brennan>Linda's line, "I'm running two companies' books in one spreadsheet." And Carla said, "We have invoices coming in on paper from farms, some of them handwritten, and they sit in a tray until someone has time."</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/41-0
00:04:37.508 --> 00:04:39.008
<v Jordan Lee>Great. Anything else?</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/42-0
00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:42.785
<v Tom Brennan>I should probably change the CRM stage, huh.</v>

b3bf9780-c9bf-5d81-b6b2-a495add9923b/43-0
00:04:43.485 --> 00:04:44.985
<v Jordan Lee>Probably. Thanks, Tom.</v>
